  <section class="tile tile--parchment center" id="services-faq">
    <div class="inner center reveal">
      <div class="eyebrow">Questions</div>
      <h2 class="metrics__h2" style="color:var(--color-ink)" data-reveal-words>Straight answers, before you ask.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="svcp-faq cs-qa" data-stagger>
      <div class="cs-qa__item reveal">
        <button class="cs-qa__head" id="sfaq-q-1" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="sfaq-a-1">
          <span class="cs-qa__qtext">How do I know you can deliver at our level?</span>
          <svg class="cs-qa__chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" /></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="cs-qa__panel" id="sfaq-a-1" role="region" aria-labelledby="sfaq-q-1">
          <div class="cs-qa__panel-inner"><p>I’ve built the reporting and approval systems a large enterprise sales operation ran on, and delivered a paying client a live profit dashboard that lifted gross profit 20%. You don’t have to take that on faith: we start with a low-risk <strong>paid diagnostic</strong>, so you see how I work and what I find before committing to a build.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-qa__item reveal">
        <button class="cs-qa__head" id="sfaq-q-2" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="sfaq-a-2">
          <span class="cs-qa__qtext">You’re one person, so what happens if you’re unavailable?</span>
          <svg class="cs-qa__chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" /></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="cs-qa__panel" id="sfaq-a-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="sfaq-q-2">
          <div class="cs-qa__panel-inner"><p>You work directly with the person who does the work, with no juniors and no hand-offs. Everything is documented: runbooks, monitoring and the source in <strong>your own repository</strong>, so your team can run it without me. For continuity, the retainer keeps a named owner on your systems, and I’ll always be honest about capacity before we start.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-qa__item reveal">
        <button class="cs-qa__head" id="sfaq-q-3" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="sfaq-a-3">
          <span class="cs-qa__qtext">Isn’t it risky to let someone automate on our live data?</span>
          <svg class="cs-qa__chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" /></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="cs-qa__panel" id="sfaq-a-3" role="region" aria-labelledby="sfaq-q-3">
          <div class="cs-qa__panel-inner"><p>That’s exactly why automation ships with a <strong>governance layer</strong>: human-in-the-loop, audit trails, rollback and edge-case handling, validated in a UAT-and-hardening phase before it touches production. For sensitive or regulated-adjacent decisions I lead with dashboards or forecasting first, where the blast radius is lower.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-qa__item reveal">
        <button class="cs-qa__head" id="sfaq-q-4" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="sfaq-a-4">
          <span class="cs-qa__qtext">Why you, and not a contract analyst or a big consultancy?</span>
          <svg class="cs-qa__chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" /></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="cs-qa__panel" id="sfaq-a-4" role="region" aria-labelledby="sfaq-q-4">
          <div class="cs-qa__panel-inner"><p>A contractor takes a spec and bills days. A large firm puts juniors behind a partner. You get one senior person who <strong>diagnoses the problem, owns the outcome, and hands over a documented system</strong>: fixed scope, no layers, no day-rate clock and no RFP.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-qa__item reveal">
        <button class="cs-qa__head" id="sfaq-q-5" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="sfaq-a-5">
          <span class="cs-qa__qtext">Why start with a paid diagnostic instead of a proposal?</span>
          <svg class="cs-qa__chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" /></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="cs-qa__panel" id="sfaq-a-5" role="region" aria-labelledby="sfaq-q-5">
          <div class="cs-qa__panel-inner"><p>Because I won’t quote a build blind. The diagnostic quantifies the cost of the problem in <em>your</em> numbers and produces a written spec with acceptance criteria, so the build is fixed-scope and de-risked for both of us. The fee is <strong>credited in full</strong> against the build.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-qa__item reveal">
        <button class="cs-qa__head" id="sfaq-q-6" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="sfaq-a-6">
          <span class="cs-qa__qtext">How do you price, and why fixed scope?</span>
          <svg class="cs-qa__chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" /></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="cs-qa__panel" id="sfaq-a-6" role="region" aria-labelledby="sfaq-q-6">
          <div class="cs-qa__panel-inner"><p>Builds are value-priced against the outcome and scoped from the diagnostic, not billed by the day. Fixed scope with a change-order clause means the price holds, and my speed is my problem to solve, not your cost to carry.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-qa__item reveal">
        <button class="cs-qa__head" id="sfaq-q-7" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="sfaq-a-7">
          <span class="cs-qa__qtext">Is our data safe? What about GDPR?</span>
          <svg class="cs-qa__chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" /></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="cs-qa__panel" id="sfaq-a-7" role="region" aria-labelledby="sfaq-q-7">
          <div class="cs-qa__panel-inner"><p>I’ll sign an NDA on request, work with least-privilege access and on a copy where possible, and delete data on completion. For any automated decisioning I build in the human oversight and audit trail GDPR Article 22 expects.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-qa__item reveal">
        <button class="cs-qa__head" id="sfaq-q-8" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="sfaq-a-8">
          <span class="cs-qa__qtext">What happens after handover?</span>
          <svg class="cs-qa__chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" /></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="cs-qa__panel" id="sfaq-a-8" role="region" aria-labelledby="sfaq-q-8">
          <div class="cs-qa__panel-inner"><p>You own the source, the runbooks and a documented, monitored system, with a defined support window. Keep it in-house, or take the retainer and I’ll maintain and evolve it: capacity without a full-time hire.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================== CONTACT CTA (dark) — Services page version ===================== -->
  <section class="tile tile--dark cta" id="services-book">
    <div class="inner center reveal">
      <h2 class="cta__h2">Let’s see if I can <span class="accent">help</span>.</h2>
      <p class="cta__sub">Tell me what’s breaking, roughly what it’s costing, and what you’ve tried. If it’s a fit, we start with a paid diagnostic; if it isn’t, I’ll say so and point you somewhere better.</p>
      <div class="cta__book">
        <a class="pill pill--primary cta__submit" {...bookAttrs} data-magnetic>Book a discovery call</a>
        <p class="cta__reassure">Engagements start with a paid diagnostic (from €1,500, credited to your build). If you need a few hours of ad-hoc analysis, I’m probably not the right fit, and I’ll happily point you to someone who is.</p>
        <p class="cta__resource">Prefer to scope it out first? <a href="#">Grab the project brief</a>, or see <a href="#">how working together works</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cta__or" aria-hidden="true"><span class="cta__or-line"></span>or send a message<span class="cta__or-line"></span></div>
      <form class="cta__form" id="contactFormServices" action="https://formsubmit.co/muriloarielreis@gmail.com" method="POST" novalidate>
        <input type="hidden" name="_subject" value="New enquiry from your portfolio site (Services page)" />
        <input type="hidden" name="_captcha" value="false" />
        <input type="hidden" name="_template" value="table" />
        <input type="text" name="_honey" style="display:none" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" aria-hidden="true" />
        <input class="cta__field" type="text" name="name" placeholder="Your name" aria-label="Your name" autocomplete="name" required />
        <span class="cta__err" id="err-services-name" aria-live="polite"></span>
        <input class="cta__field" type="email" name="email" placeholder="Work email" aria-label="Work email" autocomplete="email" required />
        <span class="cta__err" id="err-services-email" aria-live="polite"></span>
        <input class="cta__field" type="text" name="role" placeholder="Your role (e.g. COO, Head of Ops, Finance)" aria-label="Your role" autocomplete="organization-title" />
        <select class="cta__field" name="budget" aria-label="Which fits best (optional)">
          <option value="">Which fits best? (optional)</option>
          <option value="Diagnostic (from €1,500)">Diagnostic (from €1,500)</option>
          <option value="Build (€8k&ndash;€30k)">Build (€8k&ndash;€30k)</option>
          <option value="Retainer (from €2,000/mo)">Retainer (from €2,000/mo)</option>
          <option value="Not sure yet">Not sure yet</option>
        </select>
        <select class="cta__field" name="timeline" aria-label="Timeline (optional)">
          <option value="">Timeline (optional)</option>
          <option value="Now / this month">Now / this month</option>
          <option value="This quarter">This quarter</option>
          <option value="Just exploring">Just exploring</option>
        </select>
        <textarea class="cta__field" name="message" placeholder="The problem in your own words, what it’s costing, and what you’ve already tried." aria-label="Message" required></textarea>
        <span class="cta__err" id="err-services-message" aria-live="polite"></span>
        <button class="pill pill--ghost-dark cta__submit" type="submit">Send a message</button>
        <div class="cta__status" id="contactStatusServices" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>
      </form>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
